WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.130
I'll talk about Bernie Sanders in a little
bit.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:07.330
But very, very soon after Bernie's endorsement
of 20 20 Democratic presidential nominee Joe

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:12.510
Biden, former President Barack Obama has now
endorsed former V.P.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.710
Joe Biden.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.289
There are people saying Obama should have
gotten involved earlier.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:21.119
I think it was pretty clear Obama was never
going to endorse Bernie.

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:25.919
And in the end, the guy Obama would likely
have endorsed one anyway.

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:32.470
So the conversation about is Obama late seems
practically speaking, irrelevant.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.950
But let's take a look to just a little bit
of Barack Obama's statement yesterday.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.860
I believe it was a 12 minute statement in
total.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.610
We'll look about look at about a minute and
a half here.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:46.030
I'm so proud to endorse Joe Biden for president
of the United States.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:49.540
Choosing Joe to be my vise president was one
of the best decisions I ever made.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.210
And it became a close friend.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:57.380
And I believe Joe has all the qualities we
need in a president right now.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.880
He's someone whose own life has taught him
how to persevere, how to bounce back when

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.100
you've been knocked down.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:09.119
When Joe talks with parents who've lost their
jobs, we hear the son of a man who once knew

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:13.460
the pain of having to tell his children that
he'd lost his.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.960
When Joe talks about opportunity for our kids,
we hear the young father who took the train

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:22.490
home each night so he could tuck his children
into bed.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.499
And we hear the influence of Jill, a lifelong
teacher.

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:33.149
When Joe talks to families who've lost a hero,
we hear another parent of an American veteran,

00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:40.429
a kindred spirit, somebody whose faith has
endured the hardest loss there is.

00:01:40.429 --> 00:01:41.429
That's Joe.

00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:47.929
Through all his trials, he's never once forgotten
the values or the moral fiber that his parents

00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:50.009
passed on to him.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.389
And that made him who he is.

00:01:52.389 --> 00:01:59.049
That's what steals his faith in God, in America
and in all of us, certainly filled with lots

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:00.490
of political speak.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.209
That to me, it it speaks to me very, very
little.

00:02:03.209 --> 00:02:06.450
It doesn't speak to me very strongly for lack
of a better term.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.130
But Barack Obama's involvement is potentially
very important here.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:14.640
Whatever you think about Barack Obama or Joe
Biden.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:21.590
A highly involved Barack Obama improves the
chances that Donald Trump is defeated.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:29.210
You might remember back in 2008, George W.
Bush was very unpopular and was almost completely

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:33.730
missing from the campaign trail in support
of the Republican nominee.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.930
John McCain just didn't make sense.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.730
It was possibly going to hurt John McCain
to have George W. Bush heavily involved in

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.790
the 2008 Republican campaign for the presidency.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:47.600
Ultimately, McCain lost anyway to Barack Obama.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.530
In this case, it's very, very different.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.630
If and when the real campaigning is able to
get going and this will depend on the virus,

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:58.760
of course, there may be a window there between,
you know, early July through late September

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.820
or maybe before Wave 2 is likely to hit where
there will be some real campaigning.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:08.070
I believe it's a very good thing for Joe Biden,
for Barack Obama to be right there with them.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:13.120
And for better or worse, Obama there with
Biden will create the contrast in people's

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.900
minds of Trump versus what things were like
under Barack Obama.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.660
Now, I want to be really clear about what
I mean by that.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:24.850
Barack Obama was wrong on many issues, right?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.090
The Obama administration's dealing with whistleblowers
was not good.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:34.090
The Obama administration's drone warfare policy
was not good way we could go on and on.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:43.300
But the U.S. was respected as an adult, was
leading us back then because we had an adult

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.900
leading us and with the country shut down.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.940
It's very difficult to gain any momentum if
you're Joe Biden.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:55.210
Trump is making bad decisions daily with coronavirus,
but sadly, many of his followers seem to fall

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.810
more and more in love with Trump, the worse
his decisions on coronavirus are.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.070
Some even see Trump as decisive and strong
and powerful in the context of virus.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.020
So Biden needs to do something to get attention
and start building momentum.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.620
OK, I guess eventually there are going to
be debates.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:13.650
We don't know exactly what the format will
be again because of the virus.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:19.290
But one way to maybe start building momentum
to a small degree would be to see Barack Obama's

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.380
increased involvement.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.550
Barack Obama, of course, much more powerful
on social media than Joe Biden.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.750
And I've said it before and I've said it many
times.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.330
The choice is just really clear.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.910
And there are people on Twitter talking about
how do you choose between two Nazis?

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.030
Don't you just opt out?

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.410
This is not a choice between two Nazis.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:44.260
This is a choice between a lunatic authoritarian
who is in way over his head, cares only about

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:49.350
himself and whose decisions are leading to
more corona virus deaths than were necessary

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.920
or than what the minimum could have otherwise
been.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.280
That's one option.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:59.190
The other option is a center left diplomat
with decades of experience who is less progressive

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.520
than I would like the president to be.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.940
The courts alone are enough to show us the
importance of voting for Biden.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:11.470
When you compare Biden and Trump on the environment,
Biden is way better when you compare Biden

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:14.060
and Trump on regulating business.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.060
Biden's better.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.580
Biden's tax plan is better.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.880
Biden's health insurance plan is better.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.740
Biden's better on LGBT rights.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:21.990
Biden's better on abortion.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.220
And on and on and on.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.770
There's just no comparison.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.460
I don't need Joe to come beg for my vote.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:32.340
I know that there's a lot of Bernie supporters
saying Joe needs to come get my vote, but

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:38.410
Joe needs to put out a policy platform which
we can analyze like adults and make decisions

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:39.410
about.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:42.660
I don't need to try to get anybody's attention
by claiming, you know, I might stay home,

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.330
I might do it or I might write in somebody
else.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.470
It's not a blank check to the Democratic Party.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:48.930
I'm not even a Democrat.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:54.760
It's that I've looked at the policy platforms
and Biden's the clear better choice.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.650
Biden isn't entitled to anything.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:58.960
The DNC is not entitled to anything.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.730
I don't vote blue no matter who.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:01.800
I'm not a Democrat.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.139
I'm looking at the candidates.

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:05.430
It's clear which one is better.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.840
That's all this is now.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:13.060
In the meantime, a former Republican congressman,
Justin Amash, who left the Republican Party

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:20.520
and became an independent, Justin Amash, is
reportedly thinking about running as an independent.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:26.380
This would be tremendously useful to Joe Biden
and potentially damaging to Donald Trump.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:32.620
Amash, as a longtime Republican, would likely
pull way more Republican votes than he polls

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.010
Democratic votes.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.350
And being from Michigan, which could end up
being a very important state in the twenty,

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.040
twenty November election.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.560
Michigan's governor even being sort of thrown
around as a possible running mate for Joe

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.630
Biden.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:48.120
It could be a absolutely delightful thing
and could singlehandedly hand Michigan to

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.120
Joe Biden.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.300
Just a rumor that Justin Amash is thinking
about that.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:07:12.880
I say we encourage him

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:29.870
to run.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:50.690
I think

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:57.080
it's a very, very good idea.

